{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '248,518p'\"","aggregated_output":"   248\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-20.1\"\n   249\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   250\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   251\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   252\t     [yrt.escape \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   253\t     [yrt.float \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   254\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   255\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   256\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   257\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   258\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n   259\t    :yang.prelude/emitter\n   260\t    {:mode :linear                 ;; :linear (definitions->uast) | :balanced (balanced-definitions->uast)\n   261\t     :uninit :py/uninit\n   262\t     :rt-namespaces #{\"py.rt\" \"py.b\"}\n   263\t     :unshadow-locals? false\n   264\t     :finalize-c1? true            ;; annotate :yang/call-site per current module emitter\n   265\t     :capture-safe-primitives nil} ;; optional for bundled clj mode\n   266\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil  ;; optional effect-ceiling set; nil = derive without extra ceiling\n   267\t    :yang.prelude/refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"}\n   268\t   ```\n   269\t2. **`:yang.prelude/profile` (immutable, content-addressed runtime profile after publication):**\n   270\t   Replaces the recipe's local build knobs with the **published content address of the owning runtime module itself** (`:yang.prelude/root-address`) alongside the pinned transitive closure:\n   271\t   ```clojure\n   272\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   273\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   274\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-20.1\"\n   275\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   276\t    :yang.prelude/root-address \"<blake3-address-of-published-py-module>\"\n   277\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   278\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   279\t     [yrt.escape \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   280\t     [yrt.float \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   281\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   282\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   283\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   284\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   285\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n   286\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil} ;; optional allowed-effect ceiling (e.g., the verified Python closure's #{:cell/new :cell/get :cell/set! :cell/authentic? :cell/new-provenance :cell/provenance}); nil = derive from verified closure without an extra ceiling\n   287\t   ```\n   288\t   A `:yang.prelude/profile` contains zero host functions or closures and passes `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`. Its `:yang.prelude/root-address` ensures two profiles cannot claim identical identity while pointing at different owning prelude definitions.\n   289\t\n   290\t### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n   291\t\n   292\t`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks:\n   293\t\n   294\t1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):**\n   295\t   - Admission takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an **immutable, verified map `{address -> verified-manifest}`** (never assuming a graph from bare `[sym addr]` pairs!).\n   296\t   - Separately checks **direct root pins** and the **transitive closure**:\n   297\t     - Every `[sym addr]` in `:yang.prelude/components` and `:yang.prelude/root-address` resolves in `artifact-store`, and the root manifest's direct `:requires` map matches `:yang.prelude/components` (pinning direct edges without requiring transitive-only dependencies such as `clj.bridge` via `clojure.core` to be duplicated at the root).\n   298\t     - Recursively walks every `:requires` edge starting from `:yang.prelude/root-address` across `artifact-store`, verifying that every transitively reachable address resolves, that the full transitive `:requires` DAG is finite and acyclic, and that no two distinct addresses bind the same linker module symbol anywhere in the closure.\n   299\t2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):**\n   300\t   - Distinct Layer-2a/2b modules **may** share identical bare local export names (for instance, `yrt.float/abs` and `py/abs` coexist safely across qualified module borders).\n   301\t   - Collisions **are refused** whenever two components bind the same linker module symbol, when a local `module-definitions` key collides after namespace stripping, or when two source-facing `:ambient-projections` claim the same target identifier (`§6.3`).\n   302\t3. **Provenance-door security exclusion:**\n   303\t   - Validation verifies that no `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, or Layer-2c (e.g., `clojure.core`) manifest in the closure exports any `dsg__*` symbol or declares `:cell/new-provenance` or `:cell/provenance` in its derived effects.\n   304\t4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):**\n   305\t   - Rather than duplicating the manifest's derived effect set (honoring \"Derive, don't persist\"), `:yang.prelude/max-effects` is strictly optional. When present, admission checks `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` and refuses if any transitive module or host declaration exceeds the ceiling.\n   306\t5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):**\n   307\t   - Because `yin.vm.module/register-host-module` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:249`) stores exports and profiles without retaining raw limit declarations (`yin.vm.integer` does not export `integer/max-bits`, and `yang.python.antlr.prelude/register-integer-module:4163` validates an explicit `limits` map before registration), **`admit-profile` takes `(profile artifact-store registry host-limits)`**.\n   308\t   - Verifies that `registry` supplies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`) AND verifies every declared floor in `:yang.prelude/host-modules` (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) against the trusted composition `host-limits` map (failing closed if `host-limits` is absent or below the required floor, and cross-checking `integer/max-digits` / `data/max-items` against `host-limits` when present).\n   309\t6. **Dual-emitter preservation & Parity Law:**\n   310\t   - **Linked emission:** derives `:requires` and `:skip?` from `:yang.prelude/components`, emits `require` nodes in declared order, preserves `:rt-namespaces`, runs optional local unshadowing (`php`), and preserves exact C1 finalization (`:finalize-c1?` — matching `py`, `js`, `clj`, `yang.call` today while keeping `php` consistent).\n   311\t   - **Bundled emission (`compose-bundled`):** preserves existing ordering, `init!` placement, tail-marking, `:mode` (`:linear` vs `:balanced`, never silently altered because tree shape is content-addressed), and Clojure's custom preamble / `dsg__*` wrapper.\n   312\t   - **Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law:** Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n   313\t\n   314\t---\n   315\t\n   316\t## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n   317\t\n   318\tMaking Layer-2a components reusable solves code duplication; making **Layer-2b/2c preludes swappable libraries** solves syntax-to-runtime coupling. A frontend like `yang.python` can then treat its runtime prelude as a pluggable library (`:yang.semantics/descriptor`).\n   319\t\n   320\t### 6.1 Level 1 vs. Level 2 library composition\n   321\t\n   322\t- **Level 1 — Ambient Library Projection:** Keep the frontend's native semantics (`py`, `js`, `php`) and link an external module (such as `clojure.core`) into its ambient lookup scope via `yang.call`.\n   323\t- **Level 2 — Pluggable Semantics Library:** Replace the frontend's lowering contract itself with a compatible prelude library (e.g., compiling Python syntax against `clojure.core` + `clj` directly onto persistent Yin data structures with zero value wrapping or marshalling).\n   324\t\n   325\tLevel 2 strictly subsumes Level 1: a semantics descriptor defines **both** what lowering emits for syntax constructs (`:yang.semantics/hooks` + `:yang.semantics/literals`) and which ambient modules/identifiers enter source scope (`:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` + `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`).\n   326\t\n   327\t### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n   328\t\n   329\tTo preserve `yang.antlr.md` §3 (\"Yang core contains no enumeration of supported languages\"):\n   330\t- **`yang.core.semantics` (language-agnostic)** owns ONLY:\n   331\t  1. Generic schema validation for `:yang.semantics/descriptor`.\n   332\t  2. Pure, closed literal-strategy emission (`:raw`, `:float64-raw`, `:tagged-map`, `:raw-or-call`).\n   333\t  3. Generic capability lookup, hook-hygiene validation (every hook must be namespace-qualified), exact export verification against the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure** across **every** executable descriptor field (hooks, executable literal strategies such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`, and ambient projections), and reserved-door projection checks.\n   334\t- **Each frontend package (e.g. `yang.python.antlr.contract`)** owns:\n   335\t  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n   336\t  2. Structural AST lowering rules (e.g., how Python functions, loops, comprehensions, module packets, and `try`/`except`/`else`/`finally` marshal operands to those hooks).\n   337\t\n   338\t`yang.core.semantics` validates a descriptor **against the frontend-supplied contract table** — core never hardcodes Python, JS, or PHP syntax constructs.\n   339\t\n   340\t### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n   341\t\n   342\tA semantics descriptor contains **only portable data** (satisfies `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`):\n   343\t\n   344\t```clojure\n   345\t{:yang.semantics/schema 1\n   346\t :yang.semantics/id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   347\t :yang.semantics/syntax :python\n   348\t :yang.semantics/prelude-module 'clj.py\n   349\t :yang.semantics/ambient-modules\n   350\t [{:module 'yang.call,     :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   351\t  {:module 'yrt.escape,    :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   352\t  {:module 'yrt.float,     :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   353\t  {:module 'yrt.int,       :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   354\t  {:module 'clj,           :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   355\t  {:module 'clj.bridge,    :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   356\t  {:module 'clojure.core,  :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n   357\t  {:module 'clj.py,        :address \"<blake3-address>\"}]\n   358\t\n   359\t :yang.semantics/capabilities\n   360\t {:mutation/locals      :cell          ;; :cell | :single-assignment | :refused\n   361\t  :mutation/subscript   :refused       ;; :supported | :refused\n   362\t  :mutation/attribute   :refused\n   363\t  :mutation/delete      :refused\n   364\t  :scope/global         :supported     ;; per-module globals cell only\n   365\t  :scope/nonlocal       :supported     ;; lexical cells when :mutation/locals is :cell\n   366\t  :calls/positional     :supported\n   367\t  :calls/varargs        :supported     ;; *args\n   368\t  :calls/defaults       :refused\n   369\t  :calls/kwonly         :refused\n   370\t  :calls/kwstar         :refused\n   371\t  :calls/kwargs         :refused\n   372\t  :destructuring/unpack :refused       ;; explicit choice; or :supported via clj.py/unpack\n   373\t  :expr/comprehensions  :supported     ;; eager list/set/dict only; genexpr gated by :control/generators\n   374\t  :control/exceptions   :supported     ;; bare `except:` + `finally` + `raise` (`except Exc as e:` requires :control/except-typed; `except as e:` is invalid Python 3 grammar)\n   375\t  :control/except-typed :refused       ;; class-matched / typed `except ExcType [as e]:` refused when :oo/classes :refused\n   376\t  :control/generators   :refused       ;; gates BOTH `yield`/`yield from` AND generator expressions\n   377\t  :control/with         :refused\n   378\t  :oo/classes           :refused\n   379\t  :modules/import       :ambient-only} ;; :supported | :ambient-only | :refused\n   380\t\n   381\t :yang.semantics/literals\n   382\t {:nil     {:kind :raw, :value nil}\n   383\t  :bool    {:kind :raw}\n   384\t  :str     {:kind :raw}\n   385\t  :float   {:kind :float64-raw}      ;; vs {:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}\n   386\t  :int     {:kind :raw-or-call, :safe-max-bits 53, :overflow-op 'clj.py/int-lit}\n   387\t  :unbound {:kind :raw, :value :clj/unbound}}\n   388\t\n   389\t :yang.semantics/hooks\n   390\t {;; Arithmetic & comparisons — ALL namespace-qualified (hygienic, immune to guest shadowing)\n   391\t  :op/add           'clj.py/add\n   392\t  :op/sub           'clj.py/sub\n   393\t  :op/mul           'clj.py/mul\n   394\t  :op/truediv       'clj.py/truediv\n   395\t  :op/floordiv      'clj.py/floordiv\n   396\t  :op/mod           'clj.py/mod\n   397\t  :op/pow           'clj.py/pow\n   398\t  :op/neg           'clj.py/neg\n   399\t  :op/pos           'clj.py/pos\n   400\t  :op/eq            'clj.py/eq\n   401\t  :op/ne            'clj.py/ne\n   402\t  :op/lt            'clj.py/lt\n   403\t  :op/le            'clj.py/le\n   404\t  :op/gt            'clj.py/gt\n   405\t  :op/ge            'clj.py/ge\n   406\t  :op/lnot          'clj.py/lnot\n   407\t  :op/truthy        'clj.py/truthy\n   408\t  ;; Collections, indexing, and comprehension accumulators\n   409\t  :coll/vconj       'clj.py/vconj\n   410\t  :coll/list        'clj.py/list\n   411\t  :coll/tuple       'clj.py/tuple\n   412\t  :coll/set         'clj.py/set-from\n   413\t  :coll/dict        'clj.py/map-from\n   414\t  :coll/getitem     'clj.py/get-item\n   415\t  :comp/list-new    'clj.py/comp-list-new    ;; [init-vec] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/list\n   416\t  :comp/list-append 'clj.py/comp-list-append ;; [acc val] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/list-append\n   417\t  :comp/set-new     'clj.py/comp-set-new     ;; [] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/set-new\n   418\t  :comp/set-add     'clj.py/comp-set-add     ;; [acc val] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/set-add\n   419\t  :comp/dict-new    'clj.py/comp-dict-new    ;; [] -> accumulator; py-v1: 'py/dict-new\n   420\t  :comp/dict-set    'clj.py/comp-dict-set    ;; [acc k v] -> step result; py-v1: 'py/dict-set\n   421\t  :comp/finish      'clj.py/comp-finish      ;; optional [acc] -> final collection; nil in py-v1\n   422\t  ;; Scopes & bindings\n   423\t  :env/local-get    'clj.py/local-get\n   424\t  :env/global-get   'clj.py/global-get\n   425\t  :env/global-set   'clj.py/global-set\n   426\t  ;; Functions & calls\n   427\t  :fn/arg           'clj.py/arg\n   428\t  :fn/make          'clj.py/make-fn\n   429\t  :fn/call          'clj.py/call\n   430\t  ;; Control flow & unit entry\n   431\t  :ctrl/for-each    'clj.py/for-each\n   432\t  :ctrl/try         'clj.py/try\n   433\t  :ctrl/try-finally 'clj.py/try-finally\n   434\t  :ctrl/raise       'clj.py/raise\n   435\t  :ctrl/call-ec     'clj.py/call-ec\n   436\t  :unit/run-main    'clj.py/run-main}\n   437\t\n   438\t ;; Each entry defaults to :kind :cell-accessor (resolves `(m/e)` to obtain the\n   439\t ;; module's stable task-local authenticated callable cell); optional :kind :value\n   440\t ;; reads an immutable non-callable export directly.\n   441\t :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n   442\t {\"identity\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'identity,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n   443\t  \"inc\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'inc,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   444\t  \"dec\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'dec,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   445\t  \"str\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'str,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   446\t  \"count\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'count,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   447\t  \"first\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'first,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   448\t  \"rest\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'rest,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   449\t  \"second\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'second,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   450\t  \"cons\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'cons,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   451\t  \"conj\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'conj,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   452\t  \"assoc\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   453\t  \"assoc_in\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'assoc-in,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n   454\t  \"get\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   455\t  \"get_in\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'get-in,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   456\t  \"update\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   457\t  \"update_in\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'update-in, :kind :cell-accessor}\n   458\t  \"map\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   459\t  \"filter\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'filter,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   460\t  \"reduce\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'reduce,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   461\t  \"into\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'into,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   462\t  \"keys\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'keys,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   463\t  \"vals\"      {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vals,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   464\t  \"merge\"     {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'merge,     :kind :cell-accessor}\n   465\t  \"is_empty\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'empty?,    :kind :cell-accessor}\n   466\t  \"is_nil\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'nil?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   467\t  \"is_map\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'map?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   468\t  \"is_vector\" {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'vector?,   :kind :cell-accessor}\n   469\t  \"is_set\"    {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'set?,      :kind :cell-accessor}\n   470\t  \"ex_info\"   {:module 'clj.py,       :export 'ex-info,   :kind :cell-accessor}}}\n   471\t```\n   472\t\n   473\t### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and address neutrality\n   474\t\n   475\t1. **Hygienic generated references (no bare hook symbols):**\n   476\t   - Every symbol in `:yang.semantics/hooks` (when non-nil, e.g., optional `:comp/finish`) and every literal-strategy call symbol (such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`) **MUST be namespace-qualified** (e.g., `clj.py/vconj`, `py/vconj`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/int-lit`). Unqualified symbols (such as bare `conj`, `+`, `not`, `set`) are rejected at validation (`:yang.semantics/unqualified-hook`), because bare symbols inside lowered UAST could be silently captured by a valid Python parameter or local named `conj` or `not`.\n   477\t2. **Scope-aware precedence for `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`:**\n   478\t   - Free source identifiers resolve in strict order:\n   479\t     1. **Lexical scope** (`:local`, `:cell`, `:nonlocal` parameter or local variable, including a local named `map` or `conj`),\n   480\t     2. **Per-module globals** (`globals` dictionary via `:env/global-get`, allowing module-level `def` or `global` assignment to shadow an ambient binding cleanly),\n   481\t     3. **`:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`** (resolved via `clj.py/global-get` fallback to the module's explicit projected lookup map, calling `(m/e)` for `:kind :cell-accessor` entries, or refused at runtime/admission if absent).\n   482\t   - Defining or binding a parameter named `conj` or `is_empty` shadows only that source lookup and **never** alters compiler-generated calls to `clj.py/vconj`, `clj.py/add`, etc.\n   483\t3. **Exact export & reserved-door authority validation against the selected closure (`validate-descriptor`):**\n   484\t   - Takes `(descriptor frontend-contract artifact-store registry)`:\n   485\t     - Computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**: every `[module address]` in `:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` must resolve in `artifact-store` along with its full transitive `:requires` DAG (with unique module-symbol bindings).\n   486\t     - Inspects **every executable reference anywhere in the descriptor**: every active hook in `:yang.semantics/hooks` (including non-nil optional hooks such as `:comp/finish`), every executable literal-strategy field (such as `:yang.semantics/literals.*.overflow-op`), and every `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` target (`{:module m :export e}`).\n   487\t     - Verifies every such symbol is namespace-qualified (for hooks and literal strategies), matches the frontend-authorized role and arity in `frontend-contract`, and exists as an **exact published export in the selected, address-verified closure** (or in a host module of `registry` explicitly required by that selected closure and permitted by `frontend-contract`, or an allowed non-reserved VM primitive). An export belonging to an unrelated manifest somewhere else in `artifact-store` outside the descriptor's selected closure is **rejected**!\n   488\t     - For `:ambient-projections`, checks unique source names and, when `:kind :cell-accessor` (the default), verifies that module `m` exports both the named 0-arg accessor `e` and its idempotent task table initializers (`init!`, `export`).\n   489\t     - **Reserved-door ban:** Refuses any descriptor whose `:hooks`, executable `:literals.*` fields, or `:ambient-projections` references `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal adapter entries (`clojure.core/raw-*`), or exposes any unprivileged raw primitive without projection. Registry availability never grants source-level authority.\n   490\t   - Any violation fails closed before reading CST packets with `:yang.semantics/invalid-descriptor`.\n   491\t4. **Fail-closed capability enforcement during lowering:**\n   492\t   - Before lowering any guarded CST construct (e.g., `classdef`, `yield_expr`, `genexpr`, `with_stmt`, `del_stmt`, typed `except E:` / `except E as e:`, keyword argument call, default parameter value, subscript assignment), the lowering checks the descriptor's capability map.\n   493\t   - Generator expressions MUST check `:control/generators` (so they cannot evade generator refusal even when `:expr/comprehensions` is `:supported`).\n   494\t   - Any disabled/absent capability emits:\n   495\t     ```clojure\n   496\t     {:status :refused\n   497\t      :reason :yang.semantics/unsupported-capability\n   498\t      :capability :oo/classes\n   499\t      :semantics-id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   500\t      :construct \"classdef\"\n   501\t      :node <cst-node-id>}\n   502\t     ```\n   503\t5. **Byte-identical default-profile invariant (`P2`, zero golden churn for decoupling):**\n   504\t   - Refactoring `yang.python.antlr.lower` (in **Slice P2** — and subsequently TypeScript/PHP) to read from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` MUST emit **byte-identical UAST rows** under the default descriptor (`:yang.python/py-v1`, carrying all `py/*` hooks including `:comp/list-new 'py/list`, `:comp/list-append 'py/list-append`, `:comp/set-new 'py/set-new`, `:comp/set-add 'py/set-add`, `:comp/dict-new 'py/dict-new`, `:comp/dict-set 'py/dict-set`, `:comp/finish nil`, `{:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}`, `{:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/str}`, `:py/None`, and existing supported capabilities) compared to the pre-refactor hardcoded lowering. Zero existing golden addresses move in P2.\n   505\t\n   506\t### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n   507\t\n   508\tNo `yang.frontend` schema change is required (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`):\n   509\t- `:yang.frontend/id` continues to name the frontend syntax + lowering implementation (e.g., `:yang.python/antlr`), and each distinct configuration receives a distinct immutable `:yang.frontend/revision` (e.g., `\"py-v1\"` vs. `\"clojure-core-v1\"` — re-installing `[id revision]` with a different manifest returns `:yang.frontend/revision-conflict`).\n   510\t- `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile` pins the content address of the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` EDN artifact.\n   511\t- `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the content address of the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest.\n   512\t- Compilation provenance records `(cst-address, lowering-profile, runtime-profile, unit-address)` as data; note that distinct descriptors may legitimately yield identical UAST addresses on simple programs (many-to-one), so provenance retains the exact compilation tuple rather than inferring the descriptor from the UAST address alone.\n   513\t\n   514\t---\n   515\t\n   516\t## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n   517\t\n   518\tThis section specifies the reference cross-paradigm profile in full, reconciling Python's lowering ABI, 4-host numeric portability, cross-unit callable admission, §8.10.7 exception bridging, and a portable `clojure.core` module.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
