{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc | sed -n '49,204p;270,321p;379,482p;575,671p'\"","aggregated_output":"    49\t     `::float-overflow`. `compare-float` compares an integer with a\n    50\t     float exactly, -1, 0 or 1, never rounding the integer: the caller\n    51\t     excludes NaN, and an infinity compares by its sign. `from-float`\n    52\t     truncates a finite float toward zero, exactly. Each is one\n    53\t     algorithm over the shim, never a host conversion of a big integer.\n    54\t   - The float text exports (version 4) use no host float parser or\n    55\t     printer. `float-digits` answers `[digits exp10]` for a finite\n    56\t     nonzero float `v`: `digits` is the shortest decimal string, no\n    57\t     leading or trailing zero, that reads back to `v`, the closest to\n    58\t     `v` among the shortest (CPython's `repr` digits), and |v| is\n    59\t     d1.d2...dn x 10^exp10; zero, NaN and infinity are the caller's to\n    60\t     exclude. `decimal->float` is CPython's `float(str)` after syntax:\n    61\t     `digits x 10^exp10` for one or more ASCII digits and any exact\n    62\t     integer exponent, rounded once to nearest with ties to even and\n    63\t     non-negative; it answers `+inf` past the range and `0.0` below it,\n    64\t     never a limit reason, and `::max-digits` never applies to its text.\n    65\t     `max-digits` answers the composition's `::max-digits`.\n    66\t   - `pow` raises to a non-negative exponent exactly, by squaring.\n    67\t   - `parse` reads an optional `-` and one or more digits of `radix` (2\n    68\t     to 36, default 10, either letter case) exactly, never through a\n    69\t     float or a native-width parser. Signs other than `-`, prefixes,\n    70\t     underscores and whitespace are the prelude's syntax, not this\n    71\t     kernel's. `format` writes exact lowercase text, a `-` only when\n    72\t     negative, no prefix.\n    73\t\n    74\t   Limits (ruling 11) are explicit composition data with no default, in\n    75\t   bits and digits: `::max-bits` bounds the bit length of every integer\n    76\t   result, and `::max-digits` bounds the digit count `parse` reads and\n    77\t   `format` writes in a radix that is not a power of two. A result that\n    78\t   would breach `::max-bits` is refused before it is built wherever its\n    79\t   size is known in advance (`mul`, `shift-left`, `pow`).\n    80\t\n    81\t   A limit breach is returned, not thrown (version 2): the call answers\n    82\t   the keyword `::bit-limit` or `::digit-limit` in place of its result,\n    83\t   and a float result that is not finite answers `::float-overflow`\n    84\t   (version 3). Every other result is an integer, a float, a boolean, a\n    85\t   string or a pair, so the sum needs no tag, and a pair is never\n    86\t   answered with one half refused. A guest prelude translates the three\n    87\t   reasons into catchable guest exceptions; the Python profile maps\n    88\t   `::bit-limit` to `MemoryError` and `::digit-limit` to `ValueError`,\n    89\t   never `OverflowError` (`py/int-result`), and its translator must\n    90\t   learn `::float-overflow`, which is CPython's `OverflowError`, \\\"int too\n    91\t   large to convert to float\\\".\n    92\t\n    93\t   Every other refusal throws `ex-info` with the message\n    94\t   `refusal-message` and ex-data built here, never host exception text,\n    95\t   never an operand: `::op`, `::reason` and the reason's own keys. These\n    96\t   reasons are `:arity`, `:wrong-type`, `:out-of-range`, `:syntax`,\n    97\t   `:zero-division`, `:negative-count` and `:negative-exponent`: a\n    98\t   caller checks for them before the call, so reaching one is a defect\n    99\t   of the caller, and it stays a host failure, never a guest\n   100\t   exception.\"\n   101\t  (:require\n   102\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n   103\t    [dao.host.float :as float-kernel]\n   104\t    [dao.host.integer :as host]\n   105\t    [yin.vm :as vm]\n   106\t    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(def module-name\n   110\t  \"The module `register-integer-module` installs.\"\n   111\t  'integer)\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(def module-version\n   115\t  \"The version of the kernels' contract. A change to any export's\n   116\t   semantics is a new version. Version 2 returns the limit reasons\n   117\t   instead of throwing them; version 3 adds `to-float`, `compare-float`,\n   118\t   `true-div`, `from-float` and the `::float-overflow` reason, and the\n   119\t   native fast paths inside `add`, `sub`, `mul` and `compare`, whose\n   120\t   results are unchanged; version 4 adds the float text kernels\n   121\t   `float-digits` and `decimal->float`, and `max-digits`, every version 3\n   122\t   semantic unchanged.\"\n   123\t  4)\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\t(def refusal-message\n   127\t  \"The message of every refusal an `integer` export throws.\"\n   128\t  \"integer primitive refused\")\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- refuse!\n   132\t  [op reason data]\n   133\t  (throw (ex-info refusal-message (merge {::op op, ::reason reason} data))))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn- wrong-type!\n   137\t  \"Refuse argument `arg` (0-based) of `op`, which must be `expected`.\"\n   138\t  [op arg expected]\n   139\t  (refuse! op :wrong-type {::arg arg, ::expected expected}))\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t;; =============================================================================\n   143\t;; Promotion, demotion and limits\n   144\t;; =============================================================================\n   145\t\n   146\t(def ^:private zero (host/from-native 0))\n   147\t(def ^:private one (host/from-native 1))\n   148\t(def ^:private neg-one (host/from-native -1))\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\t(defn- big!\n   152\t  \"Argument `arg` of `op` promoted to the host big integer, or a\n   153\t   `:wrong-type` refusal.\"\n   154\t  [op arg x]\n   155\t  (if (host/exact-integer? x)\n   156\t    (host/promote x)\n   157\t    (wrong-type! op arg :integer)))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- sign\n   161\t  [b]\n   162\t  (host/compare-big b zero))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(defn- bits\n   166\t  [b]\n   167\t  (host/magnitude-bit-length b))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn- out\n   171\t  \"Big integer result `b` in its canonical carrier, or `::bit-limit`.\"\n   172\t  [limits b]\n   173\t  (if (> (bits b) (::max-bits limits))\n   174\t    ::bit-limit\n   175\t    (host/demote b)))\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t(defn- pair\n   179\t  \"`[q r]`, or the first of them that is a limit reason.\"\n   180\t  [q r]\n   181\t  (cond (keyword? q) q\n   182\t        (keyword? r) r\n   183\t        :else [q r]))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t;; =============================================================================\n   187\t;; Arithmetic\n   188\t;; =============================================================================\n   189\t\n   190\t(defn- int-add\n   191\t  [limits a b]\n   192\t  (out limits (host/add (big! 'add 0 a) (big! 'add 1 b))))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(defn- int-sub\n   196\t  [limits a b]\n   197\t  (out limits (host/sub (big! 'sub 0 a) (big! 'sub 1 b))))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(defn- int-neg\n   201\t  [limits a]\n   202\t  (out limits (host/sub zero (big! 'neg 0 a))))\n   203\t\n   204\t\n   270\t    (int-compare limits a b)))\n   271\t\n   272\t\n   273\t(def ^:private fast-kernels\n   274\t  {'add fast-add, 'sub fast-sub, 'mul fast-mul, 'compare fast-compare})\n   275\t\n   276\t\n   277\t(defn- divisor!\n   278\t  [op b]\n   279\t  (let [y (big! op 1 b)]\n   280\t    (when (zero? (sign y))\n   281\t      (refuse! op :zero-division {}))\n   282\t    y))\n   283\t\n   284\t\n   285\t(defn- int-quot-rem\n   286\t  [limits a b]\n   287\t  (let [x (big! 'quot-rem 0 a)\n   288\t        y (divisor! 'quot-rem b)]\n   289\t    (pair (out limits (host/quot-trunc x y))\n   290\t          (out limits (host/rem-trunc x y)))))\n   291\t\n   292\t\n   293\t(defn- int-floor-div-mod\n   294\t  [limits a b]\n   295\t  (let [x (big! 'floor-div-mod 0 a)\n   296\t        y (divisor! 'floor-div-mod b)\n   297\t        q (host/quot-trunc x y)\n   298\t        r (host/rem-trunc x y)\n   299\t        adjust? (and (not (zero? (sign r))) (not= (sign r) (sign y)))]\n   300\t    (pair (out limits (if adjust? (host/sub q one) q))\n   301\t          (out limits (if adjust? (host/add r y) r)))))\n   302\t\n   303\t\n   304\t(defn- int-pow\n   305\t  [limits a e]\n   306\t  (let [x (big! 'pow 0 a)\n   307\t        n (big! 'pow 1 e)\n   308\t        max-bits (::max-bits limits)]\n   309\t    (cond\n   310\t      (neg? (sign n)) (refuse! 'pow :negative-exponent {})\n   311\t      (zero? (sign n)) 1\n   312\t      (or (zero? (sign x)) (zero? (host/compare-big x one))) (host/demote x)\n   313\t      (zero? (host/compare-big x neg-one))\n   314\t      (if (zero? (sign (host/bit-and-big n one))) 1 -1)\n   315\t      ;; |x| >= 2 from here, so |x^n| has at least n + 1 bits\n   316\t      (pos? (host/compare-big n (host/from-native max-bits))) ::bit-limit\n   317\t      (> (inc (* (dec (bits x)) (host/to-native n))) max-bits) ::bit-limit\n   318\t      :else\n   319\t      (out limits\n   320\t           (loop [result one\n   321\t                  base x\n   379\t\n   380\t(defn- int-shift-right\n   381\t  [limits a k]\n   382\t  (let [x (big! 'shift-right 0 a)\n   383\t        n (count! 'shift-right k)]\n   384\t    (if (neg? (host/compare-big n (host/from-native (bits x))))\n   385\t      (out limits (host/shift-right-big x (host/to-native n)))\n   386\t      (if (neg? (sign x)) -1 0))))\n   387\t\n   388\t\n   389\t(defn- int-bit-length\n   390\t  [_limits a]\n   391\t  (bits (big! 'bit-length 0 a)))\n   392\t\n   393\t\n   394\t;; =============================================================================\n   395\t;; Floats (version 3)\n   396\t;; =============================================================================\n   397\t\n   398\t(def ^:private two-53-float (float-kernel/pow2 53))\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\t(defn- magnitude\n   402\t  [b]\n   403\t  (if (neg? (sign b)) (host/sub zero b) b))\n   404\t\n   405\t\n   406\t(defn- ratio->float\n   407\t  \"`dao.host.float/ratio->float`, with its overflow sentinel answered as\n   408\t   this module's `::float-overflow`.\"\n   409\t  [x y negative?]\n   410\t  (let [f (float-kernel/ratio->float x y negative?)]\n   411\t    (if (= ::float-kernel/float-overflow f) ::float-overflow f)))\n   412\t\n   413\t\n   414\t(defn- int-to-float\n   415\t  [_limits a]\n   416\t  (let [x (big! 'to-float 0 a)]\n   417\t    (ratio->float (magnitude x) one (neg? (sign x)))))\n   418\t\n   419\t\n   420\t(defn- int-true-div\n   421\t  [_limits a b]\n   422\t  (let [x (big! 'true-div 0 a)\n   423\t        y (divisor! 'true-div b)]\n   424\t    ;; CPython: 0 / -5 is -0.0\n   425\t    (ratio->float (magnitude x) (magnitude y)\n   426\t                  (not= (neg? (sign x)) (neg? (sign y))))))\n   427\t\n   428\t\n   429\t(defn- float!\n   430\t  \"Argument `arg` of `op` as a host double, or a `:wrong-type` refusal.\"\n   431\t  [op arg v]\n   432\t  (if (host/host-float? v) v (wrong-type! op arg :float)))\n   433\t\n   434\t\n   435\t(defn- int-compare-float\n   436\t  [_limits a f]\n   437\t  (let [x (big! 'compare-float 0 a)\n   438\t        v (float! 'compare-float 1 f)]\n   439\t    (cond\n   440\t      (host/nan-float? v) (wrong-type! 'compare-float 1 :non-nan-float)\n   441\t      (host/infinite-float? v) (if (pos? v) -1 1)\n   442\t      :else\n   443\t      ;; t = trunc(v): x < t means x < v, x > t means x >= t + 1 > v\n   444\t      ;; (or x > t >= v when v is negative); x = t leaves the fraction\n   445\t      (let [c (host/compare-big x (float-kernel/trunc-big v))]\n   446\t        (cond (not (zero? c)) c\n   447\t              (or (>= (float-kernel/signed (neg? v) v) two-53-float)\n   448\t                  (= v (host/native->double (host/trunc-native v))))\n   449\t              0\n   450\t              (pos? v) -1\n   451\t              :else 1)))))\n   452\t\n   453\t\n   454\t(defn- int-from-float\n   455\t  [limits f]\n   456\t  (let [v (float! 'from-float 0 f)]\n   457\t    (if (or (host/nan-float? v) (host/infinite-float? v))\n   458\t      (wrong-type! 'from-float 0 :finite-float)\n   459\t      (out limits (float-kernel/trunc-big v)))))\n   460\t\n   461\t\n   462\t;; =============================================================================\n   463\t;; Text\n   464\t;; =============================================================================\n   465\t\n   466\t(def ^:private digit-values\n   467\t  \"Each digit character, either letter case, to its value.\"\n   468\t  (into {}\n   469\t        (mapcat (fn [i]\n   470\t                  (let [c (subs \"0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\" i (inc i))]\n   471\t                    [[c i] [(str/upper-case c) i]])))\n   472\t        (range 36)))\n   473\t\n   474\t\n   475\t(defn- radix!\n   476\t  \"Radix argument `r` of `op` as a native integer from 2 to 36.\"\n   477\t  [op r]\n   478\t  (let [n (big! op 1 r)]\n   479\t    (when-not (and (<= 0 (host/compare-big n (host/from-native 2)))\n   480\t                   (<= (host/compare-big n (host/from-native 36)) 0))\n   481\t      (refuse! op :out-of-range {::arg 1, ::lo 2, ::hi 36}))\n   482\t    (host/to-native n)))\n   575\t;; Recognition\n   576\t;; =============================================================================\n   577\t\n   578\t(defn- int-integer?\n   579\t  [_limits x]\n   580\t  (host/exact-integer? x))\n   581\t\n   582\t\n   583\t(defn- int-normalize\n   584\t  [limits a]\n   585\t  (out limits (big! 'normalize 0 a)))\n   586\t\n   587\t\n   588\t;; =============================================================================\n   589\t;; The module\n   590\t;; =============================================================================\n   591\t\n   592\t(def ^:private exports\n   593\t  \"`[name arities kernel]` of every export. Each kernel takes the\n   594\t   composition's limits first.\"\n   595\t  [['integer? [1] int-integer?]\n   596\t   ['normalize [1] int-normalize]\n   597\t   ['add [2] int-add]\n   598\t   ['sub [2] int-sub]\n   599\t   ['neg [1] int-neg]\n   600\t   ['mul [2] int-mul]\n   601\t   ['compare [2] int-compare]\n   602\t   ['quot-rem [2] int-quot-rem]\n   603\t   ['floor-div-mod [2] int-floor-div-mod]\n   604\t   ['pow [2] int-pow]\n   605\t   ['bit-and [2] int-bit-and]\n   606\t   ['bit-or [2] int-bit-or]\n   607\t   ['bit-xor [2] int-bit-xor]\n   608\t   ['bit-not [1] int-bit-not]\n   609\t   ['shift-left [2] int-shift-left]\n   610\t   ['shift-right [2] int-shift-right]\n   611\t   ['bit-length [1] int-bit-length]\n   612\t   ['parse [1 2] int-parse]\n   613\t   ['format [1 2] int-format]\n   614\t   ['to-float [1] int-to-float]\n   615\t   ['compare-float [2] int-compare-float]\n   616\t   ['true-div [2] int-true-div]\n   617\t   ['from-float [1] int-from-float]\n   618\t   ['float-digits [1] int-float-digits]\n   619\t   ['decimal->float [2] int-decimal->float]\n   620\t   ['max-digits [0] int-max-digits]])\n   621\t\n   622\t\n   623\t(defn- arity-checked\n   624\t  \"`f` refusing, as data, a call whose argument count `arities` does not\n   625\t   admit, so a wrong count never reaches a host arity exception.\"\n   626\t  [op arities f]\n   627\t  (let [fixed (set arities)]\n   628\t    (fn [& args]\n   629\t      (let [n (count args)]\n   630\t        (when-not (contains? fixed n)\n   631\t          (refuse! op :arity {::argc n}))\n   632\t        (apply f args)))))\n   633\t\n   634\t\n   635\t(defn- check-limits!\n   636\t  \"Refuse `limits` unless both limits are given as positive native\n   637\t   integers: the module has no default.\"\n   638\t  [limits]\n   639\t  (doseq [k [::max-bits ::max-digits]]\n   640\t    (let [v (get limits k)]\n   641\t      (when-not (and (host/exact-integer? v)\n   642\t                     (not (host/big-carrier? v))\n   643\t                     (pos? v))\n   644\t        (throw (ex-info \"integer module needs explicit limits\"\n   645\t                        {::reason :limits, ::limit k}))))))\n   646\t\n   647\t\n   648\t(defn integer-module\n   649\t  \"The `integer` module's exports under `limits`, export symbol to host\n   650\t   function. `limits` must carry `::max-bits` and `::max-digits`.\"\n   651\t  [limits]\n   652\t  (check-limits! limits)\n   653\t  (let [limits (select-keys limits [::max-bits ::max-digits])\n   654\t        ;; chosen once: every fast result fits in 53 bits\n   655\t        fast? (>= (::max-bits limits) 53)]\n   656\t    (into {}\n   657\t          (map (fn [[op arities f]]\n   658\t                 (let [f (if fast? (get fast-kernels op f) f)]\n   659\t                   [op (arity-checked op arities (partial f limits))])))\n   660\t          exports)))\n   661\t\n   662\t\n   663\t(def integer-profiles\n   664\t  \"UCF 7.5.2 profiles for the `integer` module: every export `:pure`,\n   665\t   declaring no effects and no host state.\"\n   666\t  (into {}\n   667\t        (map (fn [[op arities _]]\n   668\t               [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure arities #{} :none)]))\n   669\t        exports))\n   670\t\n   671\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
