{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | sed -n '25,115p;226,280p;354,486p'\"","aggregated_output":"    25\t;; =============================================================================\n    26\t\n    27\t(defn empty-registry\n    28\t  \"An empty module registry value.\"\n    29\t  []\n    30\t  {:modules {}, :effect-handlers {}})\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(defn- symbol->path\n    34\t  \"Split a dotted symbol into a get-in path of symbols.\n    35\t   'yin.io.file-input-stream → ['yin 'io 'file-input-stream]\"\n    36\t  [sym]\n    37\t  (mapv symbol (str/split (str sym) #\"\\.\")))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn- walk-path\n    41\t  \"Descend a registry's :modules map along path, a sequence of symbols.\n    42\t\n    43\t   Namespace segments step through plain maps until the path reaches a\n    44\t   module entry (a map carrying :manifest); the remaining segments read\n    45\t   that entry's task-local lowered `:bindings` when it holds them -- a\n    46\t   linked module (yin.vm.linker.md section 8.3) -- and its `:slice`\n    47\t   otherwise, which for a host module is the host values themselves, so\n    48\t   a binding name resolves to its export.\"\n    49\t  [node path]\n    50\t  (if (seq path)\n    51\t    (if (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest))\n    52\t      (if-let [child (get node (first path))]\n    53\t        (walk-path child (rest path))\n    54\t        (get-in node (into [(if (contains? node :bindings) :bindings :slice)]\n    55\t                           path)))\n    56\t      (when-let [child (get node (first path))]\n    57\t        (walk-path child (rest path))))\n    58\t    node))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn module-entry\n    62\t  \"The registry entry of module `module-name` in `modules` (a registry's\n    63\t   `:modules` map), or nil when the dotted path reaches no module entry.\"\n    64\t  [modules module-name]\n    65\t  (let [node (reduce (fn [node seg] (when (map? node) (get node seg)))\n    66\t                     modules\n    67\t                     (symbol->path module-name))]\n    68\t    (when (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest)) node)))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn assoc-module\n    72\t  \"Return registry with `entry` installed as module `module-name`.\"\n    73\t  [registry module-name entry]\n    74\t  (let [registry (or registry (empty-registry))\n    75\t        path (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n    76\t        children (into {} (filter (comp symbol? key)) (get-in registry path))]\n    77\t    (assoc-in registry path (merge children entry))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn link-module\n    81\t  \"The `linked` transition's registry update (yin.vm.linker.md sections\n    82\t   7.3 and 8.3): `registry` gains the module `manifest` names as the\n    83\t   portable encoding of acts 1 to 3 -- `{:manifest m :address a\n    84\t   :derivation d :slice {sym encoded} :stores {address snapshot} :cells\n    85\t   {cell-id cell} :images {identity image}}` -- never lowered values. `a`\n    86\t   is the manifest's own address; `lifted` is the act-1 lift, `{:slice\n    87\t   :stores :cells :images}`, the cells being the logical cursor cells its\n    88\t   references name (r9) and the images the verified origin images a\n    89\t   receiving task attaches.\n    90\t   Each receiving task lowers the entry into its own `:bindings`.\"\n    91\t  [registry manifest derivation lifted]\n    92\t  (assoc-module registry\n    93\t                (:yin.module/name manifest)\n    94\t                {:manifest manifest,\n    95\t                 :address (jing/segment-key manifest),\n    96\t                 :derivation derivation,\n    97\t                 :slice (:slice lifted),\n    98\t                 :stores (:stores lifted),\n    99\t                 :cells (:cells lifted),\n   100\t                 :images (:images lifted)}))\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn module-entries\n   104\t  \"Every `[name entry]` a registry value holds, the module name read back\n   105\t   from each entry's manifest.\"\n   106\t  [registry]\n   107\t  (letfn [(walk\n   108\t            [node]\n   109\t            (when (map? node)\n   110\t              (if (contains? node :manifest)\n   111\t                (cons [(:yin.module/name (:manifest node)) node]\n   112\t                      (mapcat (comp walk val) (filter (comp symbol? key) node)))\n   113\t                (mapcat walk (vals node)))))]\n   114\t    (vec (walk (:modules registry)))))\n   115\t\n   226\t\n   227\t(defn register-host-module\n   228\t  \"Return registry with host module `module-name` installed from `fns`\n   229\t   under `profiles`.\n   230\t\n   231\t   module-name is a dotted symbol; fns maps each export symbol to the host\n   232\t   value it publishes; profiles maps each export symbol to its UCF 7.5.2\n   233\t   profile record in the shape of `yin.vm/primitive-profiles`. Every\n   234\t   binding must carry a profile, and the profile's class must be `:pure`,\n   235\t   or `:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, with\n   236\t   `:yin.k/host-state` `:none`. An `:effectful` export returns an\n   237\t   effect minted by `make-effect` for the engine to interpret and\n   238\t   performs no IO itself; `stream/make` is exactly such a constructor.\n   239\t   Each export's declared effect set is also entered in the registry's\n   240\t   identity-keyed `:callable-effects`, which the engine checks an\n   241\t   effect's kind against (D4).\n   242\t\n   243\t   The module is entered as an already-linked manifest with\n   244\t   `:yin.module/tree` absent, `:yin.module/derivations {}`, and its\n   245\t   exports listed under `:yin.module/primitives` by profile address; the\n   246\t   exports themselves are its `:slice`, and its `:address` and\n   247\t   `:derivation` are nil because no content was fetched or derived: the\n   248\t   host is the boundary.\"\n   249\t  [registry module-name fns profiles]\n   250\t  (doseq [sym (sort-by str (keys fns))]\n   251\t    (check-binding! module-name sym (get profiles sym)))\n   252\t  (-> (or registry (empty-registry))\n   253\t      (update :callable-effects\n   254\t              (partial merge-with into)\n   255\t              (vm/callable-effects fns profiles))\n   256\t      (assoc-in (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n   257\t                {:manifest {:yin.module/name module-name,\n   258\t                            :yin.module/derivations {},\n   259\t                            :yin.module/primitives\n   260\t                            (into {} (map (fn [[sym _f]]\n   261\t                                            [sym (:yin.k/profile\n   262\t                                                   (get profiles sym))]))\n   263\t                                  fns)},\n   264\t                 :address nil,\n   265\t                 :derivation nil,\n   266\t                 :slice fns,\n   267\t                 :stores {}})))\n   268\t\n   269\t\n   270\t(defn host-export-profile\n   271\t  \"The profile address host module `ns` publishes for export `name`, when\n   272\t   `qualified-sym` is `ns/name` and `registry` holds `ns` as a\n   273\t   host-registered entry (`register-host-module`'s shape, `:address`\n   274\t   nil); else nil. A linked entry never answers: the\n   275\t   `:yin.module/primitives` of a fetched manifest are the primitives that\n   276\t   module assumes, not exports it provides.\"\n   277\t  [registry qualified-sym]\n   278\t  (when (and (symbol? qualified-sym) (some? (namespace qualified-sym)))\n   279\t    (let [entry (module-entry (:modules registry)\n   280\t                              (symbol (namespace qualified-sym)))]\n   354\t(def stream-profiles\n   355\t  \"UCF 7.5.2 profiles for the v2 `stream` module's bindings. Each binding\n   356\t   is an `:effectful` pure effect constructor: it returns an effect\n   357\t   declaring the one effect kind the engine interprets, and touches\n   358\t   no stream itself.\"\n   359\t  {'make (vm/primitive-profile 'make :effectful [0 1] #{:stream/make}\n   360\t                               :none)\n   361\t   'put! (vm/primitive-profile 'put! :effectful [2] #{:stream/put} :none)\n   362\t   'cursor (vm/primitive-profile 'cursor :effectful [1] #{:stream/cursor}\n   363\t                                 :none)\n   364\t   'next! (vm/primitive-profile 'next! :effectful [1] #{:stream/next} :none)\n   365\t   'poll! (vm/primitive-profile 'poll! :effectful [1] #{:stream/poll} :none)\n   366\t   'close! (vm/primitive-profile 'close! :effectful [1] #{:stream/close}\n   367\t                                 :none)})\n   368\t\n   369\t\n   370\t(defn register-stream-module\n   371\t  \"Return registry with the v2 `stream` module registered.\n   372\t   A composition that calls this must also supply `:make-stream`, or\n   373\t   `(stream/make)` is unsupported and says so.\"\n   374\t  [registry]\n   375\t  (register-host-module registry 'stream stream-module stream-profiles))\n   376\t\n   377\t\n   378\t;; =============================================================================\n   379\t;; The `cell` module\n   380\t;; =============================================================================\n   381\t;;\n   382\t;; A cell is a mutable location in the task's `:heap`, reached by a sealed\n   383\t;; `:cell-ref` (Architect cell ruling, slice 1). These are pure effect\n   384\t;; constructors like the stream module's: they touch no heap, and the engine\n   385\t;; interprets the effects they return. The heap is VM state, so a mutation\n   386\t;; is shared by every closure over the ref and is never rolled back when a\n   387\t;; continuation is invoked (box semantics). Beside the three mutators the\n   388\t;; module publishes `authentic?`, the ruling-of-record query a caller's\n   389\t;; compiled code asks the issuer before dereferencing a cell-ref-shaped\n   390\t;; callee; it answers a boolean and changes nothing.\n   391\t\n   392\t(defn new-cell\n   393\t  [v]\n   394\t  (make-effect :cell/new {:val v}))\n   395\t\n   396\t\n   397\t(defn get-cell\n   398\t  [c]\n   399\t  (make-effect :cell/get {:cell c}))\n   400\t\n   401\t\n   402\t(defn set-cell!\n   403\t  [c v]\n   404\t  (make-effect :cell/set! {:cell c, :val v}))\n   405\t\n   406\t\n   407\t(defn authentic-cell?\n   408\t  \"The pure query the cell-ref ruling of record added: does the heap\n   409\t   issue `c` as a cell reference? The engine answers the same\n   410\t   heap+seal predicate `check-ref!` consults, as a boolean, so compiled\n   411\t   call routing can ask the issuer instead of guessing from a value's\n   412\t   shape. Non-fatal, state unchanged.\"\n   413\t  [c]\n   414\t  (make-effect :cell/authentic? {:cell c}))\n   415\t\n   416\t\n   417\t(defn new-provenance-cell\n   418\t  \"The privileged mint: allocate a fresh sealed cell holding `value` with\n   419\t   `provenance` installed in its private `:provenance` sibling, atomically.\n   420\t   `provenance` must be non-nil and is otherwise opaque to the VM. Only the\n   421\t   mint attaches provenance, and only at allocation. Not a guest surface:\n   422\t   the name is compiler-private (`dsg__`).\"\n   423\t  [value provenance]\n   424\t  (make-effect :cell/new-provenance {:val value, :provenance provenance}))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t(defn provenance-cell\n   428\t  \"The private reader: the `:provenance` a live, authenticated, marked cell\n   429\t   carries, or nil for anything else — an unmarked cell, a forged or dead\n   430\t   reference, or a non-reference. Never fatal, never mutating, and the\n   431\t   engine learns no frontend semantics from the slot. Not a guest surface:\n   432\t   the name is compiler-private (`dsg__`).\"\n   433\t  [candidate]\n   434\t  (make-effect :cell/provenance {:cell candidate}))\n   435\t\n   436\t\n   437\t(def cell-module\n   438\t  \"The `cell` module definition. Registering it is a composition step. The\n   439\t   two `dsg__` bindings are the compiler-private provenance mint and reader:\n   440\t   guest code may neither spell nor construct their names.\"\n   441\t  {'new new-cell, 'get get-cell, 'set! set-cell!, 'authentic? authentic-cell?,\n   442\t   'dsg__new-provenance new-provenance-cell,\n   443\t   'dsg__provenance provenance-cell})\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t(def cell-profiles\n   447\t  \"UCF 7.5.2 profiles for the `cell` module's bindings: each an\n   448\t   `:effectful` pure effect constructor declaring its one effect kind.\"\n   449\t  {'new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :effectful [1] #{:cell/new} :none)\n   450\t   'get (vm/primitive-profile 'get :effectful [1] #{:cell/get} :none)\n   451\t   'set! (vm/primitive-profile 'set! :effectful [2] #{:cell/set!} :none)\n   452\t   'authentic? (vm/primitive-profile 'authentic? :effectful [1]\n   453\t                                     #{:cell/authentic?} :none)\n   454\t   'dsg__new-provenance (vm/primitive-profile 'dsg__new-provenance\n   455\t                                              :effectful [2]\n   456\t                                              #{:cell/new-provenance} :none)\n   457\t   'dsg__provenance (vm/primitive-profile 'dsg__provenance\n   458\t                                          :effectful [1]\n   459\t                                          #{:cell/provenance} :none)})\n   460\t\n   461\t\n   462\t(defn register-cell-module\n   463\t  \"Return registry with the `cell` module registered.\"\n   464\t  [registry]\n   465\t  (register-host-module registry 'cell cell-module cell-profiles))\n   466\t\n   467\t\n   468\t;; =============================================================================\n   469\t;; Built-in effect handlers\n   470\t;; =============================================================================\n   471\t\n   472\t;; =============================================================================\n   473\t;; `require` lowers to the linker (yin.vm.linker.md section 7)\n   474\t;; =============================================================================\n   475\t\n   476\t(defprotocol IModuleKernel\n   477\t  \"What a kernel supplies the install child and the `linked` transition\n   478\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3). Every method is a pure function of a\n   479\t   VM value; the engine owns the phases, the kernel owns its coordinates.\"\n   480\t\n   481\t  (link-format\n   482\t    [vm]\n   483\t    \"`{:format kw :contract s}`: the format this kernel links, and the\n   484\t     execution contract it runs.\")\n   485\t\n   486\t  (spawn-module\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
