{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '862,975p;1010,1098p'\"","aggregated_output":"   862\t\n   863\t(defn- encoder\n   864\t  \"UCF 7.5.1's `encode` over values of `vm`, recording into `found` every\n   865\t   closure origin segment, module store, and cursor cell the encoding\n   866\t   reaches. A closure lifts through the kernel and names the module store\n   867\t   its body resolves against: its own `:store-of`, or `own` when it has\n   868\t   none -- a closure the child's own body made. A closure or\n   869\t   continuation another task minted refuses as `:foreign-value`: lift is\n   870\t   the only crossing, and only for the owner. Every literal map is\n   871\t   wrapped, a `:type :closure` map included, so a program's data can\n   872\t   never forge a marker. A stream or\n   873\t   cursor reference is authenticated before it is encoded (r11): its seal\n   874\t   and resource kind must verify under the emitter's own secret, or it\n   875\t   refuses as `:forged-resource-reference`; only then is it encoded,\n   876\t   without its seal, as a stream marker or a cell reference. A\n   877\t   continuation, a host object, and an unnamed host function refuse as\n   878\t   UCF 7.5.4 kinds; a heap `:cell-ref` refuses as `:cell` until the heap\n   879\t   slice lifts.\"\n   880\t  [vm own found]\n   881\t  (letfn [(encode\n   882\t            [x]\n   883\t            (cond\n   884\t              (scalar? x) x\n   885\t              ;; Host types before the map arm: a plain map carrying\n   886\t              ;; `:type :closure` is a literal and is wrapped as one.\n   887\t              (values/host-typed? x)\n   888\t              (cond\n   889\t                (not (values/owned-by? x (:owner vm)))\n   890\t                (non-portable! :foreign-value {:yin.k/hint (values/kind-of x)})\n   891\t                (values/closure? x)\n   892\t                (let [marker (module/lift-closure vm (values/payload x) encode)\n   893\t                      m (or (get marker store-of-key) own)]\n   894\t                  (swap! found (fn [acc]\n   895\t                                 (-> acc\n   896\t                                     (update :origins conj\n   897\t                                             (:yin.k/segment marker))\n   898\t                                     (update :stores conj m))))\n   899\t                  (assoc marker store-of-key m))\n   900\t                :else\n   901\t                (non-portable! :non-canonicalizable\n   902\t                               {:yin.k/hint :reified-continuation}))\n   903\t              (map? x)\n   904\t              (case (:type x)\n   905\t                (:stream-ref :cursor-ref)\n   906\t                (cond\n   907\t                  (not (authentic-ref? vm (:type x) x))\n   908\t                  (non-portable! :forged-resource-reference\n   909\t                                 {:yin.k/hint (:type x)})\n   910\t                  (= :stream-ref (:type x)) (stream-marker vm (:id x))\n   911\t                  :else {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/cursor-ref,\n   912\t                         :yin.k/cell (cell-for! vm found (:id x))})\n   913\t                :parked-continuation\n   914\t                (non-portable! :non-canonicalizable {:yin.k/hint (:type x)})\n   915\t                ;; slice 1 refuses every cell-bearing lift; copy-on-lift\n   916\t                ;; of the heap slice is slice 2\n   917\t                :cell-ref\n   918\t                (non-portable! :cell {:yin.k/hint (:id x)})\n   919\t                {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/literal,\n   920\t                 :yin.k/entries (into []\n   921\t                                      (mapcat (fn [[k v]]\n   922\t                                                [(encode k) (encode v)]))\n   923\t                                      x)})\n   924\t              (vector? x) (mapv encode x)\n   925\t              (set? x) (into #{} (map encode) x)\n   926\t              (seq? x) (apply list (map encode x))\n   927\t              (fn? x) (encode-primitive vm x)\n   928\t              :else (non-portable! :host-object\n   929\t                                   {:yin.k/hint\n   930\t                                    #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n   931\t                                       :default (str (type x)))})))]\n   932\t    encode))\n   933\t\n   934\t\n   935\t(defn- decoder\n   936\t  \"UCF 7.5.1's `decode` into `vm`'s coordinates: every map is a marker, a\n   937\t   closure lowers through the kernel, a primitive is the receiver's own\n   938\t   function under an equal profile or `:yin.k/unsatisfied`, and a stream\n   939\t   or cursor marker is a fresh reference sealed under the receiver's\n   940\t   secret to the resource `lower-resources` installed for it -- `streams`\n   941\t   maps a stream identity, `cells` a cell id, to a resource id.\"\n   942\t  [vm streams cells]\n   943\t  (letfn [(decode\n   944\t            [x]\n   945\t            (cond\n   946\t              (map? x)\n   947\t              (case (:yin.k/tag x)\n   948\t                :yin.k/literal (into {}\n   949\t                                     (map (fn [[k v]] [(decode k) (decode v)]))\n   950\t                                     (partition 2 (:yin.k/entries x)))\n   951\t                :yin.k/closure (module/lower-closure vm x decode)\n   952\t                :yin.k/primitive\n   953\t                (let [n (:yin.k/name x)\n   954\t                      entry (get (:primitives vm) n)]\n   955\t                  (if (and (some? entry)\n   956\t                           (= (:yin.k/profile x)\n   957\t                              (:yin.k/profile (vm/profile-of (:primitives vm)\n   958\t                                                             n))))\n   959\t                    (vm/primitive-function entry)\n   960\t                    (fail \"Primitive unsatisfied at the receiver\"\n   961\t                          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied,\n   962\t                           :yin.k/name n,\n   963\t                           :yin.k/profile (:yin.k/profile x)})))\n   964\t                :yin.k/stream\n   965\t                (issue-ref vm :stream-ref\n   966\t                           (get streams (:dao.stream/identity x)))\n   967\t                :yin.k/cursor-ref\n   968\t                (issue-ref vm :cursor-ref (get cells (:yin.k/cell x)))\n   969\t                (fail \"Undecodable value\"\n   970\t                      {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable,\n   971\t                       :yin.k/tag (:yin.k/tag x)}))\n   972\t              (vector? x) (mapv decode x)\n   973\t              (set? x) (into #{} (map decode) x)\n   974\t              (seq? x) (apply list (map decode x))\n   975\t              :else x))]\n  1010\t  (let [used (sort-by str (distinct (map :yin.k/cell\n  1011\t                                         (markers :yin.k/cursor-ref values))))\n  1012\t        lifted (mapv (fn [cid]\n  1013\t                       (or (get cells cid)\n  1014\t                           (fail \"Undecodable value\"\n  1015\t                                 {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable,\n  1016\t                                  :yin.k/cell cid})))\n  1017\t                     used)\n  1018\t        [state streams]\n  1019\t        (reduce (fn [[s acc] marker]\n  1020\t                  (let [ident (:dao.stream/identity marker)]\n  1021\t                    (if (contains? acc ident)\n  1022\t                      [s acc]\n  1023\t                      (let [handle (attach-stream! s marker)\n  1024\t                            [id s] (gensym s \"stream\")]\n  1025\t                        [(assoc-in s [:resources id] handle)\n  1026\t                         (assoc acc ident id)]))))\n  1027\t                [state {}]\n  1028\t                (concat (markers :yin.k/stream values)\n  1029\t                        (map :yin.k/stream lifted)))\n  1030\t        [state cell-ids]\n  1031\t        (reduce (fn [[s acc] [cid cell]]\n  1032\t                  (let [[id s] (gensym s \"cursor\")\n  1033\t                        stream-id (get streams\n  1034\t                                       (get-in cell [:yin.k/stream\n  1035\t                                                     :dao.stream/identity]))]\n  1036\t                    [(assoc-in s [:resources id]\n  1037\t                               (vm/cursor-entry stream-id\n  1038\t                                                (:yin.k/position cell)))\n  1039\t                     (assoc acc cid id)]))\n  1040\t                [state {}]\n  1041\t                (map vector used lifted))]\n  1042\t    [state streams cell-ids]))\n  1043\t\n  1044\t\n  1045\t(defn- encode-store\n  1046\t  [encode store]\n  1047\t  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(encode k) (encode v)])) store))\n  1048\t\n  1049\t\n  1050\t(defn- decode-store\n  1051\t  [decode snapshot]\n  1052\t  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(decode k) (decode v)])) snapshot))\n  1053\t\n  1054\t\n  1055\t(defn lift-slice\n  1056\t  \"Act 1 of `linked` (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3): the halted child's\n  1057\t   exports and module stores in the portable encoding. `own` is the\n  1058\t   module's manifest address. Returns `{:slice {sym encoded} :stores\n  1059\t   {address snapshot} :cells {cell-id cell} :origins #{segment}}`: one\n  1060\t   snapshot per module -- the child's own store under `own`, and every\n  1061\t   dependency store the encoding reaches as it stands in the child at\n  1062\t   halt, mutations included -- and the logical cursor cells the encoded\n  1063\t   references name. A `:store-of` with no snapshot is\n  1064\t   `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind `:missing-module-store`; any refused leaf\n  1065\t   refuses the lift.\"\n  1066\t  [child own exports]\n  1067\t  (let [found (atom {:origins #{}, :stores #{}, :cells {}, :cell-of {}})\n  1068\t        encode (encoder child own found)\n  1069\t        store (:store child)\n  1070\t        slice (into {} (map (fn [k] [k (encode (get store k))])) exports)\n  1071\t        stores (loop [stores {own (encode-store encode store)}]\n  1072\t                 (let [pending (remove #(contains? stores %)\n  1073\t                                       (sort-by str (:stores @found)))]\n  1074\t                   (if (empty? pending)\n  1075\t                     stores\n  1076\t                     (recur\n  1077\t                       (reduce\n  1078\t                         (fn [acc m]\n  1079\t                           (if-let [s (get-in child [:module-stores m])]\n  1080\t                             (assoc acc m (encode-store encode s))\n  1081\t                             (non-portable! :missing-module-store\n  1082\t                                            {store-of-key m})))\n  1083\t                         stores\n  1084\t                         pending)))))]\n  1085\t    {:slice slice,\n  1086\t     :stores stores,\n  1087\t     :cells (:cells @found),\n  1088\t     :origins (:origins @found)}))\n  1089\t\n  1090\t\n  1091\t(defn receive-module\n  1092\t  \"Acts 3 and 4 of `linked` for one receiving task (yin.vm.linker.md\n  1093\t   section 7.3): attach every origin image of `entry` the kernel does not\n  1094\t   yet hold, non-destructively; lower the resources the slice and the\n  1095\t   snapshots it instantiates reference into the task's private\n  1096\t   `:resources` (r9); lower the slice against this task's own\n  1097\t   coordinates into the entry's `:bindings`, every reference re-sealed\n  1098\t   under this task's secret (r10); and instantiate each store snapshot\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
