{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc | sed -n '1,40p;156,200p;395,503p' && rg -n 'safe-native\\\\?|exact-integer\\\\?|demote|host-float\\\\?' src/cljc/dao/host/integer.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.data\n     2\t  \"The `data` host module: pure collection and string primitives a\n     3\t   language prelude is written over (Architect ruling on mutable guest\n     4\t   objects, Q5 and Q6).\n     5\t\n     6\t   Every export is `:pure` with declared effects `#{}`. The module is not\n     7\t   part of `yin.vm/primitives`: a composition whose language runtime\n     8\t   profile names it installs it explicitly with `register-data-module`,\n     9\t   and Yin source reaches the exports as `data/count`, `data/substring`\n    10\t   and so on. Under explicit limits it also exports `max-items`, the\n    11\t   composition's sequence-size limit (`register-data-module`).\n    12\t\n    13\t   Results are identical on CLJ, CLJS and CLJD:\n    14\t\n    15\t   - Strings are indexed by code point, as Python indexes them, never by\n    16\t     the hosts' UTF-16 code units: `(data/str-length \\\"a😀\\\")` is 2 on\n    17\t     every host. An unpaired surrogate is one code point of its own.\n    18\t   - `str-compare` orders by code point, which UTF-16 unit order does not\n    19\t     for supplementary characters against U+E000 to U+FFFF.\n    20\t   - Every string call decodes its whole argument, O(n), and search is a\n    21\t     naive O(n*m) scan: a prelude loop over a string's characters calls\n    22\t     `str->code-points` once and walks the vector with `nth`, never\n    23\t     `char-at` per step.\n    24\t   - An index is any number with an integral value, so `1.0` is index 1\n    25\t     on the JVM as it is on JS and Dart, which cannot tell it from `1`.\n    26\t   - Nothing iterates a host map or a host set into an ordered result:\n    27\t     host iteration order differs by host. An ordered dict is prelude\n    28\t     code, an index map beside an order vector.\n    29\t   - A refused call throws `ex-info` with the message `refusal-message`\n    30\t     and ex-data built here, never host exception text: `::op`,\n    31\t     `::reason` (`:arity`, `:wrong-type`, `:out-of-range` or\n    32\t     `:empty-separator`), and the reason's own keys.\n    33\t\n    34\t   Key equality in `contains?`, `dissoc`, `disj`, `hash-set` and `into` a\n    35\t   set is the host's `=`, which differs for `1` and `1.0` on the JVM. A\n    36\t   runtime profile normalizes guest keys before they reach these.\"\n    37\t  (:require\n    38\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n    39\t    [dao.host.float :as float]\n    40\t    [dao.host.integer :as integer-host]\n   156\t            (= needle (subvec hay i (+ i m))) i\n   157\t            :else (recur (inc i))))))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t;; =============================================================================\n   161\t;; Collection exports\n   162\t;; =============================================================================\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn- data-count\n   165\t  [coll]\n   166\t  (if (or (nil? coll) (coll? coll))\n   167\t    (count coll)\n   168\t    (wrong-type! 'count 0 :collection)))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn- vector!\n   172\t  [op arg x]\n   173\t  (when-not (vector? x)\n   174\t    (wrong-type! op arg :vector))\n   175\t  x)\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t(defn- data-nth\n   179\t  [v i]\n   180\t  (vector! 'nth 0 v)\n   181\t  (let [i (index! 'nth 1 i)]\n   182\t    (in-range! 'nth i 0 (dec (count v)))\n   183\t    (nth v i)))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn- data-contains?\n   187\t  [coll k]\n   188\t  (cond\n   189\t    (or (nil? coll) (map? coll) (set? coll)) (contains? coll k)\n   190\t    (vector? coll) (let [i (integral k)]\n   191\t                     (boolean (and i (< -1 i (count coll)))))\n   192\t    :else (wrong-type! 'contains? 0 :map-set-or-vector)))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(defn- data-dissoc\n   196\t  [m & ks]\n   197\t  (if (or (nil? m) (map? m))\n   198\t    (apply dissoc m ks)\n   199\t    (wrong-type! 'dissoc 0 :map)))\n   200\t\n   395\t\n   396\t(defn- str-compare\n   397\t  \"-1, 0 or 1 as `a` orders before, with or after `b` by code point.\"\n   398\t  [a b]\n   399\t  (let [x (text/code-points (string! 'str-compare 0 a))\n   400\t        y (text/code-points (string! 'str-compare 1 b))\n   401\t        n (min (count x) (count y))]\n   402\t    (loop [i 0]\n   403\t      (if (< i n)\n   404\t        (let [p (nth x i)\n   405\t              q (nth y i)]\n   406\t          (cond (< p q) -1\n   407\t                (> p q) 1\n   408\t                :else (recur (inc i))))\n   409\t        (cond (< (count x) (count y)) -1\n   410\t              (> (count x) (count y)) 1\n   411\t              :else 0)))))\n   412\t\n   413\t\n   414\t;; =============================================================================\n   415\t;; Kinds\n   416\t;; =============================================================================\n   417\t\n   418\t(defn- data-number?\n   419\t  \"True when `x` is a host number or an exact-integer carrier, including\n   420\t   a JS or Dart big integer, which answers false to `number?`. A\n   421\t   closure, a continuation, nil and a map are not, whatever they answer\n   422\t   to `get`.\"\n   423\t  [x]\n   424\t  (or (number? x) (integer-host/big-carrier? x)))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t;; =============================================================================\n   428\t;; Floats: the seam between addressed float content and host arithmetic\n   429\t;; =============================================================================\n   430\t\n   431\t(defn float-value\n   432\t  \"The host double of number or float64 content `x`, for host arithmetic:\n   433\t   what the literal `1.0` is on each host, a double on the JVM and Dart, a\n   434\t   Number on JS. A prelude unwraps a float with this, computes on bare\n   435\t   numbers, and wraps the result back with `float64`.\"\n   436\t  [x]\n   437\t  (when-not (or (data-number? x) (cbor/float64? x))\n   438\t    (wrong-type! 'float-value 0 :number))\n   439\t  #?(:cljd (if (dart/is? x BigInt) (.toDouble ^BigInt x) (.toDouble ^num x))\n   440\t     :clj (double x)\n   441\t     :cljs (cond (number? x) x\n   442\t                 (cbor/float64? x) (.-v ^not-native x)\n   443\t                 :else (js/Number x))))\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t(defn float64\n   447\t  \"Float content with the value of number `x`: Jing's float64, the form a\n   448\t   float keeps in any value that can reach an addressed row or image (a\n   449\t   double on the JVM and Dart, the float64 carrier on JS, where a bare\n   450\t   integral Number is an integer; dao.jing.cbor.md, Numeric identity). The\n   451\t   producer carries float kind; the codec never infers it.\"\n   452\t  [x]\n   453\t  (cbor/float64 (float-value x)))\n   454\t\n   455\t\n   456\t(defn- callable?\n   457\t  \"True when `x` can be applied: a host function, a closure or a\n   458\t   continuation. A map is never callable, whatever keys it carries.\"\n   459\t  [x]\n   460\t  (or (fn? x) (values/closure? x) (values/continuation? x)))\n   461\t\n   462\t\n   463\t(defn- data-map?\n   464\t  [x]\n   465\t  (map? x))\n   466\t\n   467\t\n   468\t(defn- data-vector?\n   469\t  [x]\n   470\t  (vector? x))\n   471\t\n   472\t\n   473\t(defn- data-string?\n   474\t  [x]\n   475\t  (string? x))\n   476\t\n   477\t\n   478\t(defn- ref?\n   479\t  \"True when `x` is a stream, cursor or cell reference.\"\n   480\t  [x]\n   481\t  (and (map? x) (contains? #{:stream-ref :cursor-ref :cell-ref} (:type x))))\n   482\t\n   483\t\n   484\t(defn- data-content=\n   485\t  \"True when `a` and `b` have one identity under content addressing:\n   486\t   Jing's kind-strict content equality, so every NaN is one value, 0.0 is\n   487\t   not -0.0, 1 is not 1.0, and collections recurse. A callable or a\n   488\t   reference compares by host `=`, so content addressing never walks it.\"\n   489\t  [a b]\n   490\t  (or (identical? a b)\n   491\t      (if (or (callable? a) (callable? b) (ref? a) (ref? b))\n   492\t        (= a b)\n   493\t        (cbor/content= a b))))\n   494\t\n   495\t\n   496\t;; =============================================================================\n   497\t;; The module\n   498\t;; =============================================================================\n   499\t\n   500\t(def ^:private exports\n   501\t  \"`[name arities f]` of every export. `:variadic` means the greatest\n   502\t   listed fixed arity extends to further arguments.\"\n   503\t  [['count [1] data-count]\n24:   `demote` turns a result back into its canonical carrier. JavaScript\n66:(defn exact-integer?\n84:(defn safe-native?\n86:   a Dart `int`, or exactly the `Number` arm of `exact-integer?` on JS.\n101:(defn host-float?\n132:   checked `exact-integer?`.\"\n163:(defn demote\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
