{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/host/integer.cljc | sed -n '12,115p;157,187p' && nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc | sed -n '201,238p' && nl -ba src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc | sed -n '71,112p'\"","aggregated_output":"    12\t   by `dao.host.conformance-test`.\n    13\t\n    14\t   Each integer value has exactly one carrier per host:\n    15\t\n    16\t   | Host | Native carrier                      | Big carrier          |\n    17\t   |------|-------------------------------------|----------------------|\n    18\t   | JVM  | `long`, signed 64-bit               | `clojure.lang.BigInt`|\n    19\t   | JS   | `Number`, within +/-(2^53 - 1)      | host `BigInt`        |\n    20\t   | Dart | `int`, signed 64-bit                | `BigInt`             |\n    21\t\n    22\t   `promote` turns any exact-integer carrier into the host big integer\n    23\t   the operations below take (`java.math.BigInteger` on the JVM);\n    24\t   `demote` turns a result back into its canonical carrier. JavaScript\n    25\t   holds +/-2^53 as a `BigInt`, never as an unsafe `Number`, and a\n    26\t   JavaScript `-0` is floating-point content, not an integer.\n    27\t\n    28\t   The entries from `big-carrier?` to `to-radix-string` were moved\n    29\t   verbatim from the former `yin.vm.integer.host` shim (slice H1); slice\n    30\t   H2 moved its consumers here and deleted it. A refusal throws `ex-info` whose data carries\n    31\t   `:dao.host/refusal`, a class keyword, and `:dao.host/entry`. This\n    32\t   namespace requires nothing in the repository. Every reader\n    33\t   conditional names `:cljd` first, because the ClojureDart build also\n    34\t   reads `:clj`.\"\n    35\t  #?@(:cljd [(:import [\"dart:core\" BigInt]\n    36\t                      [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List])]\n    37\t      :clj [(:import (java.math BigInteger))]))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn- refuse\n    41\t  [entry cls detail]\n    42\t  (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.host refused: \" entry \" \" (name cls) \" (\" detail \")\")\n    43\t                  {:dao.host/refusal cls :dao.host/entry entry :detail detail})))\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t;; =============================================================================\n    47\t;; Recognition\n    48\t;; =============================================================================\n    49\t\n    50\t#?(:cljs\n    51\t   (defn- js-bigint?\n    52\t     [x]\n    53\t     (identical? \"bigint\" (js* \"typeof ~{}\" x))))\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(defn big-carrier?\n    57\t  \"True when `x` is a host big-integer carrier: `clojure.lang.BigInt` or\n    58\t   `BigInteger` on the JVM, a `BigInt` on JS and Dart. On JS and Dart\n    59\t   such a value answers false to `number?`.\"\n    60\t  [x]\n    61\t  #?(:cljd (dart/is? x BigInt)\n    62\t     :clj (or (instance? clojure.lang.BigInt x) (instance? BigInteger x))\n    63\t     :cljs (js-bigint? x)))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t(defn exact-integer?\n    67\t  \"True when `x` is an exact integer in any carrier the host has: a JVM\n    68\t   `long`, `int`, `short`, `byte`, `BigInt` or `BigInteger`; a JS\n    69\t   safe-integer `Number` other than `-0`, or a `BigInt`; a Dart `int` or\n    70\t   `BigInt`. A float with an integral value is not, except on JS, which\n    71\t   cannot tell `1.0` from `1`.\"\n    72\t  [x]\n    73\t  #?(:cljd (or (dart/is? x int) (dart/is? x BigInt))\n    74\t     :clj (or (instance? Long x) (instance? Integer x) (instance? Short x)\n    75\t              (instance? Byte x) (instance? clojure.lang.BigInt x)\n    76\t              (instance? BigInteger x))\n    77\t     :cljs (or (js-bigint? x)\n    78\t               (and (number? x)\n    79\t                    (js/Number.isSafeInteger x)\n    80\t                    ;; -0 is the one zero whose reciprocal is negative\n    81\t                    (not (and (zero? x) (neg? (/ 1 x))))))))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(defn safe-native?\n    85\t  \"True when `x` is a native carrier within +/-(2^53 - 1): a JVM `long`,\n    86\t   a Dart `int`, or exactly the `Number` arm of `exact-integer?` on JS.\n    87\t   Two such values add, subtract and compare natively without rounding\n    88\t   or wrapping on every host.\"\n    89\t  [x]\n    90\t  #?(:cljd (and (dart/is? x int)\n    91\t                (<= -9007199254740991 x)\n    92\t                (<= x 9007199254740991))\n    93\t     :clj (and (instance? Long x)\n    94\t               (let [n (.longValue ^Long x)]\n    95\t                 (and (<= -9007199254740991 n) (<= n 9007199254740991))))\n    96\t     :cljs (and (number? x)\n    97\t                (js/Number.isSafeInteger x)\n    98\t                (not (and (zero? x) (neg? (/ 1 x)))))))\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\t(defn host-float?\n   102\t  \"True when `x` is a host binary64: a JVM `Double`, a Dart `double`, any\n   103\t   JS `Number`.\"\n   104\t  [x]\n   105\t  #?(:cljd (dart/is? x double)\n   106\t     :clj (instance? Double x)\n   107\t     :cljs (number? x)))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn nan-float?\n   111\t  \"True when host float `x` is a NaN.\"\n   112\t  [x]\n   113\t  #?(:cljd (.-isNaN ^double x)\n   114\t     :clj (Double/isNaN (double x))\n   115\t     :cljs (js/isNaN x)))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t#?(:cljs\n   160\t   (def ^:private js-min-safe (js/BigInt -9007199254740991)))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn demote\n   164\t  \"The canonical carrier of host big integer `b`: native iff `b` is in\n   165\t   the host's native range, else the host big carrier.\"\n   166\t  [b]\n   167\t  #?(:cljd (if (.-isValidInt ^BigInt b) (.toInt ^BigInt b) b)\n   168\t     :clj (if (< (.bitLength ^BigInteger b) 64)\n   169\t            (.longValue ^BigInteger b)\n   170\t            (clojure.lang.BigInt/fromBigInteger b))\n   171\t     :cljs (if (js* \"(~{} <= ~{} && ~{} <= ~{})\" js-min-safe b b js-max-safe)\n   172\t             (js/Number b)\n   173\t             b)))\n   174\t\n   175\t\n   176\t(defn to-native\n   177\t  \"Host big integer `b` as a native integer. The caller has checked that\n   178\t   `b` lies within +/-(2^53 - 1).\"\n   179\t  [b]\n   180\t  #?(:cljd (.toInt ^BigInt b)\n   181\t     :clj (.longValue ^BigInteger b)\n   182\t     :cljs (js/Number b)))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn native->double\n   186\t  \"Native integer `n`, within +/-2^53, as a host double: exact.\"\n   187\t  [n]\n   201\t(defn- host-integer?\n   202\t  \"True for an exact integer in any host carrier, and on JavaScript also\n   203\t   for an integral Number beyond +/-(2^53 - 1), which is integer content\n   204\t   whose value is already rounded (callers refuse it); never a JS -0.\"\n   205\t  [x]\n   206\t  (or (integer/exact-integer? x)\n   207\t      #?(:cljs (and (number? x) (js/Number.isInteger x)\n   208\t                    (not (js/Number.isSafeInteger x)))\n   209\t         :default false)))\n   210\t\n   211\t\n   212\t(defn float64?\n   213\t  \"True for floating-point content: Double or Float on the JVM, the\n   214\t   Float64 carrier or a non-integral, non-finite or negative-zero number\n   215\t   on JavaScript, a double on Dart.\"\n   216\t  [x]\n   217\t  #?(:cljd (dart/is? x double)\n   218\t     :clj (or (instance? Double x) (instance? Float x))\n   219\t     :cljs (or (instance? number/Float64 x)\n   220\t               (and (number? x) (not (host-integer? x))))))\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\t(defn decimal?\n   224\t  \"True for decimal content: BigDecimal on the JVM, the Decimal carrier on\n   225\t   JavaScript and Dart.\"\n   226\t  [x]\n   227\t  (number/decimal? x))\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn ratio?\n   231\t  \"True for rational content: clojure.lang.Ratio or the Rational carrier.\"\n   232\t  [x]\n   233\t  (number/ratio? x))\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\t(defn numeric?\n   237\t  \"True for every value the portable numeric operations accept.\"\n   238\t  [x]\n    71\t                          (str (when (< b 16) \"0\") (.toString b 16)))\n    72\t                       (range 8))))))\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t#?(:cljs\n    76\t   (deftype Float64\n    77\t     [v]\n    78\t\n    79\t     Object\n    80\t\n    81\t     (toString [_] (str v))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t     ;; numeric and default coercion refuses: `carrier + 1`, `carrier < 3`\n    85\t     ;; and `\"\" + carrier` would otherwise go through toString and answer\n    86\t     ;; a string or a bare Number that lost the float's kind. String\n    87\t     ;; conversion (`str`, `String`, `.toString`) asks toString first and is\n    88\t     ;; unaffected; read the value through an explicit accessor instead.\n    89\t     (valueOf\n    90\t       [_]\n    91\t       (refuse 'Float64 :carrier-coercion\n    92\t               \"a float64 carrier has no implicit numeric value\"))\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t     IEquiv\n    96\t\n    97\t     (-equiv\n    98\t       [_ other]\n    99\t       (and (instance? Float64 other)\n   100\t            (or (and (js/isNaN v) (js/isNaN (.-v ^Float64 other)))\n   101\t                (js/Object.is v (.-v ^Float64 other)))))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t     IHash\n   105\t\n   106\t     (-hash [_] (hash (if (js/isNaN v) \"nan\" (double-bits-hex v))))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t     IPrintWithWriter\n   110\t\n   111\t     (-pr-writer\n   112\t       [_ writer _]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
