ves resolves through a composition-supplied registry value, not a global\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:568:Store operations are VM-level primitives that interact directly with the global heap or \"store\". They provide mechanisms for state management and unique ID generation.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:682:- **Roots:** the kernel's registers (`IModuleKernel/gc-roots`), the store and every module store, `:parked`, `:wait-set`, `:ready-queue`, the value being boxed, and every pinned cell. Code, images, the registry, primitives and `:resources` are not roots.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/register-vm.md:41:store/primitives/module resolution. This is a correctness bug.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc:218:(defn resolve-name\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:967:;; `yin.vm.engine/resolve-var` uses: free env -> store -> primitives ->\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:1034:   `obligations` against `receiver` (`{:free-env :store :primitives\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:1962:   receiving VM's free-name environment `{:free-env :store :primitives\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1084:   `prelude` as its only primitives, no store, no module resolver, no stream\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:117:  \"Look up a variable name: env -> store -> primitives -> module registry.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:125:  [env store primitives registry name]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
